n temporal changes of the carbon balance for the studied ecosystems. The annual absorption of carbon by the peatland ecosystems of the key site "Bakcharsky" with an area of 212 thousand hectares is about 3 × 105 tons. Conclusion. Peatland ecosystems of the southern-taiga subzone of West Siberia are currently a constant sink of carbon and, as such, being sustainable natural formations, contribute to climate change mitigation.	2026-10-30 00:20:19.063034+05
