bable that the Paleozoic deposits of the East Siberian platform can be traced as they plunge to the west. In the opinion of V . G. Vasil’yev, a marginal downwarp of the East Siberian platform is probably present in this region, passing toward the west into contemporaneous Caledonian deposits of the basement of the West Siberian platform. If he is right, then the Lower Paleozoic deposits of the East Siberian platform, which are present beneath the Meso-Cenozoic cover of the West Siberian platform in the left bank area of the Yenisei, are of great interest for exploration for new oil and gas fields. There are also several interesting objectives for exploration drilling along the left bank area of the Yenisei River. Abundant gas showings recorded during drilling of exploration wells on the Malokhet structure in the Ust’-Yenisei depression and also at several other localities indicate the possibility for finding gas fields here. This would be very important to the industry of the Norilsk region. It should be noted that the volume of regional investigations and exploration in this area is extremely inadequate. The discovery of oil fields in the center of the West Siberian Lowland is n ot only of economic importance but also of great	2026-10-30 00:20:19.063034+05
